      "data": {
        "label": "Goal Review Task",
        "nodeType": "text_input",
        "properties": {
          "message": "Assess the current execution’s requested outcome using the originating instruction, ordered user corrections, and supplied action results or observations. The task model’s objective and completion criteria are interpretations of that request. Commands describe requested actions; correlated receipts and observations describe recorded results. Conversation entries retain their speaker and time and are not physical measurements. Missing evidence remains unknown. This review assesses the existing objective; Active Operator owns selection of new autonomous activities. Return outcome, reason, objective, completionCriteria, requiredCompletionBasis, observationSummary, and completionEvidence. This assessment is supplied to the final conversation model as context; Goal Review does not publish a user-facing response. Outcomes are complete, wait, request_user, or abandon. complete means the supplied evidence establishes the requested outcome; completionEvidence identifies that evidence. Other outcomes describe the existing objective’s unresolved state. Optional visualObservation interprets attached images at their recorded times. Return only the requested JSON.\n\noutcome contains the internal objective-lifecycle decision and is not spoken. completionEvidence identifies supplied observations or receipts; a cancelled command does not establish distance travelled or the number of completed gait cycles.\n\nobjective and completionCriteria describe the goal after this review and may revise its previous description using the supplied context. The original instruction and recorded results remain preserved. outcome:abandon removes the goal from active consideration without reporting success. This assessment updates goal state; it does not start actions or generate a reply.",
          "inputKey": ""
        }
      }
    },
